# Auto-managed working directory: cloned repo + the expensive mapper cache.
# Keep it on disk (it is hours of compute) but out of version control.
# The package re-clones the exercises repo itself if ecc_energy_study/ is wiped.
ecc_energy_study/timeloop-accelergy-exercises/
ecc_energy_study/outputs/
ecc_energy_study/problems/
ecc_energy_study/problems_multimodel/
ecc_energy_study/arch_*_patched*.yaml
ecc_energy_study/globals.yaml

# Generated workload shapes -- rebuild with `python3 -m eccenergy.generate`
ecc_energy_study/model_layers.json
ecc_energy_study/transformer_layers.json

# Figures, tables and manifests are reproducible from results*/_raw/ + run.sh
# (`bash hpc/sweep.sh <axis>`). Raw energies and evaluation JSONs ARE kept:
# they are the expensive part. The pattern covers every results directory
# (results/, results_noc_*/, anything ECC_RESULTS_DIR points at in here).
results*/figures/
results*/tables/
results*/manifests/

# Runtime scratch: CACTI inputs/outputs bound writable into the read-only
# image (hpc/tl.sh), and the container's temp directory.
hpc/.runtime/
tmp/

# Home-directory files that came along with the container/laptop transfer,
# not project files (the container uses this directory as $HOME).
.bashrc
.profile
.config/
.ipython/
.jupyter/
.local/

# Apptainer image (1.9 GB) -- built with `apptainer pull`, see hpc/HIPERGATOR.md §3
*.sif

# Python caches, SLURM job output (hpc/logs/*.out) and editor files are
# covered by the repository-root .gitignore; kept here too so this directory
# still behaves when copied out on its own.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# prompt_6 phase 1 probe scratch (paths.ert_probe_dir); regenerated by eccenergy.experiments.ert_probe
ecc_energy_study/ert_probe/

# Generated per run, like globals.yaml and arch_*_patched*.yaml above.
ecc_energy_study/globals_*.yaml

# The restructure gate's scratch. `restructure/` was removed on 2026-09-13,
# once phases 0-7 were done and its last permanent inhabitants (gen_guards.py,
# scaffold_arch.py) had moved to tools/. These stay so that restoring the
# directory -- from Energy_Modeling/: `git log -- restructure` -- does not also
# restore its scratch as untracked noise.
restructure/.fresh/
restructure/.trial*/
restructure/.mut/

# Pre-edit snapshots from earlier sessions (`.preC` = before prompt_7 phase C).
# The 19 that existed were archived to legacy/preC-snapshots-2026-09-13.tar.gz
# and removed on 2026-09-13; git history holds the committed states anyway.
*.preC
*.bak-*

# The archived NoC runs keep their raw energies and evaluation JSONs; their
# figures/tables/manifests are reproducible, like every other results tree.
legacy/results_noc_*/figures/
legacy/results_noc_*/tables/
legacy/results_noc_*/manifests/
